WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.771 --> 00:00:04.938
- [Narrator] Welcome to
Oregon's Big Foot Highway.

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.662
For decades maybe even
longer, people have ventured

00:00:08.662 --> 00:00:10.906
into the mountains and
woods outside of Portland

00:00:10.906 --> 00:00:14.906
to prove that mankind is
not alone in the woods.

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:19.917
(men howling)

00:00:25.576 --> 00:00:28.362
(man howling)

00:00:28.362 --> 00:00:31.242
Okay, so far mankind hasn't yet proved

00:00:31.242 --> 00:00:33.010
that Bigfoot exists.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:36.374
But for one club of long
time intrepid Bigfooters,

00:00:36.374 --> 00:00:38.707
the truth is still out there

00:00:41.017 --> 00:00:43.274
and its a great excuse to go camping.

00:00:43.274 --> 00:00:45.774
(men howling)

00:00:47.646 --> 00:00:50.436
Joe Beelart believes in
the existence of Bigfoot.

00:00:50.436 --> 00:00:51.622
He wrote a book about it.

00:00:51.622 --> 00:00:54.114
And he claims to have had
more than one sighting.

00:00:54.114 --> 00:00:56.126
- In the second instance, he was here to

00:00:56.126 --> 00:00:58.043
your cameraman from me.

00:00:59.349 --> 00:01:02.554
But I got to say I don't
think he was quite as hairy.

00:01:02.554 --> 00:01:04.757
When people are skeptical, I tell them

00:01:04.757 --> 00:01:07.209
they're like UFOs and ghosts.

00:01:07.209 --> 00:01:09.080
People see them but
there's no widely accepted

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.497
scientific proof.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.447
- [Narrator] Joe is not alone.

00:01:13.447 --> 00:01:16.715
He belongs to a group he dubs
the Clackamas Sasquatchians.

00:01:16.715 --> 00:01:19.102
Clackamas for the county he lives in.

00:01:19.102 --> 00:01:20.440
- [Joe] We're actually
in the heart land of

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:22.024
Bigfoot activity.

00:01:22.024 --> 00:01:24.960
- [Narrator] And
Sasquatchians for Sasquatch.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:29.492
- Bigfoot and Sasquatch
are synonymous terms.

00:01:29.492 --> 00:01:31.243
In my group we're Bigfooters.

00:01:31.243 --> 00:01:34.172
We just go out and do the job.

00:01:34.172 --> 00:01:36.049
- We put ourselves out there.

00:01:36.049 --> 00:01:38.139
We make a bunch of noise,
play a bunch of music

00:01:38.139 --> 00:01:41.440
and let the landscape
know that we're there

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:44.578
and then later, in the evening
that's when the strangest

00:01:44.578 --> 00:01:45.935
things would take place.

00:01:45.935 --> 00:01:48.085
Something's walking around your tent

00:01:48.085 --> 00:01:50.087
and its like, what is that?

00:01:50.087 --> 00:01:51.746
- And that's the excitement of it.

00:01:51.746 --> 00:01:54.921
Give you the heebie jeebies (laughs).

00:01:54.921 --> 00:01:56.936
- [Narrator] Their backgrounds are varied.

00:01:56.936 --> 00:02:00.917
PhDs, ex-military, a
retired science teacher.

00:02:00.917 --> 00:02:02.721
And a few engineers.

00:02:02.721 --> 00:02:05.107
And most have a specialty.

00:02:05.107 --> 00:02:08.640
- My specialty is putting out offerings.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:10.993
If you come back and there's
something laying there

00:02:10.993 --> 00:02:13.600
where that apple was, then probably it was

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.017
one of our barefoot friends.

00:02:17.264 --> 00:02:19.552
- I would like to set up a
camp in a comfortable position.

00:02:19.552 --> 00:02:21.290
I don't try to chase them down.

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:22.897
I don't try to make a lot of noise.

00:02:22.897 --> 00:02:24.713
Maybe they make a hooray of some kind,

00:02:24.713 --> 00:02:28.852
but is it a Sasquatch
that's making these noises?

00:02:28.852 --> 00:02:30.128
We didn't see it.

00:02:30.128 --> 00:02:31.492
We can't say that for sure.

00:02:31.492 --> 00:02:32.353
But its a great hobby.

00:02:32.353 --> 00:02:33.860
(distant howling)

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:35.002
- That sounded Squatchy.

00:02:35.002 --> 00:02:37.314
I mean I don't feel any
Squatchy vibes but...

00:02:37.314 --> 00:02:40.228
- Well as far as my specialty
with Joe's club is concerned,

00:02:40.228 --> 00:02:41.416
I just get a vibe.

00:02:41.416 --> 00:02:43.274
And I can tell when they're around.

00:02:43.274 --> 00:02:44.710
Usually they put out a vibe

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:47.126
and I'm really sensitive to that.

00:02:47.126 --> 00:02:49.459
- This is Squatchy for sure.

00:02:53.838 --> 00:02:55.655
- [Narrator] Whether the
Squatchy vibes are flowing

00:02:55.655 --> 00:02:59.008
is besides the point
for the Sasquatchians.

00:02:59.008 --> 00:03:02.613
The point is they are together
in their favorite place.

00:03:02.613 --> 00:03:04.508
- Why do I love doing this?

00:03:04.508 --> 00:03:08.665
The flora and the fauna, the butterflies,

00:03:08.665 --> 00:03:12.088
the night sky, its all up there.

00:03:12.088 --> 00:03:13.822
- People ask me if I believe in Bigfoot,

00:03:13.822 --> 00:03:16.935
and I never give a definitive answer.

00:03:16.935 --> 00:03:21.708
But Bigfoot is in my mind
10% of everything that we do

00:03:21.708 --> 00:03:24.208
to enjoy each other's company.

00:03:25.129 --> 00:03:27.462
- Bigfooting helped me kick the cancer

00:03:27.462 --> 00:03:30.363
spending four months in a hospital,

00:03:30.363 --> 00:03:32.707
getting chemotherapy was hell

00:03:32.707 --> 00:03:36.039
and what made me get through
that was imagining me

00:03:36.039 --> 00:03:40.193
getting me back up to the
woods and visiting my friends.

00:03:40.193 --> 00:03:41.539
Hopefully I'll get Bigfoot sitting around the

00:03:41.539 --> 00:03:43.631
campfire with me one day.

00:03:43.631 --> 00:03:46.381
(pleasant music)

